Guard JSHTMLMediaElementCustom.cpp with ENABLE(VIDEO), like its siblings.

The file defines visitAdditionalChildren for JSHTMLMediaElement, and
HTMLMediaElement.idl carries [Conditional=VIDEO] -- so with the media stack
off (this port has no GStreamer, so ENABLE_VIDEO is OFF) the generated
JSHTMLMediaElement.h still exists but declares nothing, and the build stops
with

    error: 'JSHTMLMediaElement' has not been declared

Every other custom binding for a conditional interface wraps its whole body
in the matching #if -- JSTrackCustom.cpp, in the same directory, is the exact
pattern followed here, down to the placement after "config.h" and the bare
#endif at the end of the file.  This one is simply missing it; the file is
new (its copyright reads 2026) and was written against a build where VIDEO is
always on.

Upstream: not reported yet.  Unlike the rest of this port's patches this one
is not LikeOS-specific -- it is a plain build fix for ENABLE_VIDEO=OFF and
belongs upstream as-is.

--- a/Source/WebCore/bindings/js/JSHTMLMediaElementCustom.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/bindings/js/JSHTMLMediaElementCustom.cpp
@@ -24,6 +24,9 @@
  */
 
 #include "config.h"
+
+#if ENABLE(VIDEO)
+
 #include "JSHTMLMediaElement.h"
 
 #include "TrackOpaqueRoot.h"
@@ -39,3 +42,5 @@ void JSHTMLMediaElement::visitAdditionalChildren(Visitor& visitor)
 DEFINE_VISIT_ADDITIONAL_CHILDREN(JSHTMLMediaElement);
 
 } // namespace WebCore
+
+#endif // ENABLE(VIDEO)
